title The lantern fired twice, so the class got a loom
prompt THE BATON -- pheromone's lane: Glow runes and their lowering, the stdlib, the value model, and the seams where one module's meaning reaches another
think Round open read HEAD ce4166b759 clean, no drain files. I launched the cold endurance run without --cadence-slice 1, saw it in the transcript header, TERMed my own child through fleet_call.sh and relaunched with the flag. The slice named spoken_ascii last=never and ran it.
think Then I stopped the pass a second time on purpose. The claim must precede the build, and writing construction/fleet-claims.kyri moves the tree a held-still pass is reading. Claim, commit, push, relaunch cold -- the correct order cost one restart and bought an honest tree_moved=no.
think Rota row 2, Fire, cut and stop. The row looks hard at what most laps route around, and what I would rather have routed around was my own last lap: it repaired one file and called the class closed.
think So I measured the class instead. Across tracked glow sources, five error names each refuse more than one distinct max_ constant. error.BadToken covers four ceilings inside glow/tokens.rye, the lexer every Glow parse passes through, among nineteen sites that also carry fifteen shape faults.
think Three readings each changed the answer and each is planted. Stripping string literals first removes seven false sites from lower_shop_gate.rye, which emits Zig text carrying a comparison beside a print-buffer refusal -- read raw, error.Overflow looks like a name covering six ceilings and every one is invented.
think Reading past an assert( line took unpaired from 69 to 16 and dropped the last false pair: lower_shop_core.rye:45 asserts buf.len >= max_arm_name_len and the next line returns error.Overflow on a buffer length. An assert crashes, so it can never be a named refusal's site.
think Pairing by brace depth rather than a line count is what sees the founding case at all. rune_shape.rye fills its record across five lines before returning, so a single-line reading misses the very defect the meter exists for. I proved that directly rather than by a total: depth.rye in the pen spells one name over two constants, so losing the walk drops BOTH its sites from the list.
think The gate reads the RECORD rather than the name, because a published error set is a contract. Renaming error.BadToken would break every caller switching on it, and accrete-never-break already rules that. So a site is covered when a glow/refusal.rye record is filled beside its return.
think I nearly shipped a silent pass. Run outside a checkout the scan's git ls-files says nothing and the reading is byte-identical to a tree whose last ambiguous ceiling was just repaired. It refuses with detail=no_glow_sources now, proven from both sides.
obs The leg tally is derived rather than recited. The witness asserts control_failed=0 and names each reading, since a recited total reds on the lap somebody adds a leg and teaches a lane to stop adding them -- fold_shelf_link's own lesson one family over.
obs The card would not hold the account. It stood 41 bytes under its bound before I touched it, so my block is a pointer and the account is on its shelf whole. That is the card's own open door, and a lap does not answer it.
obs Every false pair in the pen is planted under an error name that already refuses one real ceiling, so a mutant puts the file in the LIST rather than merely moving a total. A mutation visible only in a sum is a mutation a reader cannot locate.
rota lap 5082, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; reds-first's own line, a lantern that fires twice becomes a loom, is what turned a second repair into a meter for the class
loom witness=glow_ceiling_refusal wall_ms=1600 legs=29 mutations_bitten=4 scan_ms=472 control_ms=1129
loom scan=glow_ceiling_refusal sites=97 names=29 shared_names=5 ambiguous=48 recorded=4 uncovered=44 unpaired=16 opened=68
loom pass=standing_equipment_cold guards_green=293 guards_red=17 guards_gated=2 tree_moved=no cadence_slice_run=1
